#  Day 18/50 — Network Topologies

Not every network is connected in the same way.
Some devices connect to a central point, some form a circle, and others connect through multiple paths.

These arrangements are called **network topologies**

Star, Bus, Ring, Mesh and Tree are some common types.

Each structure has its own advantages and limitations.
The way devices are arranged can affect performance, reliability and how easily the network can grow

It's interesting how the same devices can work differently just because their connections are arranged differently.
Even in a group, structure matters.

Who connects to whom, how information flows, and what happens when one connection fails can change everything.

**Sometimes, it's not just about having connections. It's about how those connections are arranged.**
